<div class="section-label jump-target" id="current-status">Current Status</div>
<h2>What Is Known Now</h2>

<p>The SR-177 Weber County extension segment from 1800 North to 4000 South is in the State Environmental Study phase.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %} UDOT has not published a final approved preferred alignment or final parcel-level right-of-way boundary through the formal State Environmental Study materials as of October 28, 2026. UDOT has scheduled the Draft State Environmental Study, which it says identifies a Preferred Alternative, for online publication on November 6, 2026.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %}</p>

<div class="callout info">
  <p><strong>Technical source note:</strong> Public ArcGIS working layers reviewed May 23, 2026 include a <code>21158 Hybrid Concept Design</code> group and ROW-related feature-service metadata.{% cite "arcgis-sr177-webmap-may2026" %}{% cite "arcgis-sr177-project-layers-may2026" %}{% cite "arcgis-sr177-row-service-may2026" %} Treat those layers as evidence that technical design work is underway, not as final property guidance or a formal preferred-alternative decision.</p>
</div>

