<div class="section-label jump-target" id="decision-points">Decision Points</div>
<h2>Where the Timeline Becomes Actionable</h2>

<p>The next major public milestone is the Draft State Environmental Study, scheduled for online publication on November 6, 2026. UDOT says it identifies a Preferred Alternative, and it should provide the first formal alignment maps for the Weber County segment.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %} The formal comment period runs from November 6 through December 11, 2026.{% cite "udot-ses-public-hearing-nov2026" %}</p>

<ul style="margin: 16px 0 20px 24px; line-height: 1.8;">
  <li><strong>Online informational presentation:</strong> Monday, November 9, 2026, 6–7 p.m. Register on the study page to receive the link.{% cite "udot-ses-online-presentation-nov2026" %}</li>
  <li><strong>Official in-person public hearing:</strong> Tuesday, November 10, 2026, 4:30–7:30 p.m., at Roy Junior High School, 5347 South 2100 West, Roy. It is an open house with no formal presentation; attendees can talk with the study team and give formal comments.{% cite "udot-ses-public-hearing-nov2026" %}</li>
  <li><strong>Neighborhood meetings:</strong> invitation-only meetings for property owners and tenants affected by planned impacts, held separately in early November 2026.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %}</li>
  <li><strong>Final State Environmental Study:</strong> listed for late 2026 or early 2027, after UDOT responds to comments.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %}</li>
</ul>

<p>This schedule is consistent with the July 15, 2026 report to the West Haven City Council that UDOT was moving toward completing the study before November 2026.{% cite "whc-warnke-minutes-jul2026" %}</p>

